  <static seed="62" source="Library/Union/setMVvectors/an12_2_31.pg">
    <statement><p>Suppose <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;u\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt; = \left\lt 3,0\right&gt;</m> and <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt; = \left\lt 3,-9\right&gt;</m> are two
vectors that form the sides of a parallelogram.  Then the lengths of
the two diagonals of the parallelogram are
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
<p><em> Separate answers with a comma.
</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>9, 10.8167</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The diagonals are given by</p>
<p><m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;u\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;+\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt; = \lt 3,0&gt; + \lt 3,-9&gt; = \lt 6,-9&gt;</m> and 
<m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;u\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;-\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt; = \lt 3,0&gt; - \lt 3,-9&gt; = \lt 0,9&gt;</m>.</p>
<p>Their lengths are 
<m>\sqrt{(6)^2+(-9)^2} = \sqrt{117}</m> and 
 <m>\sqrt{(0)^2+(9)^2}=\sqrt{81}</m>, respectively.</p>
</solution>
